@Concerned Citizen If you look at causes for unprepared students and our dumbed down education system though it points back to parents. Parents play a much smaller role in education than they used to since family dynamics have changed so much over the years. For students to succeed in school they need to study, read, and practice-which requires both and in and out of school effort.
When kids go home and forget homework playing video games all night; they surely are going to fail the test. When they fail the test the logical person to blame is the student and parents for not working on study habits, but the parents will come into school demanding their child get a better grade because its not fair-even when other students in the class got good grades because they paid attention in class and studied. This teaches their child that they don't need to work hard to get by, and it forces the teacher into a position where she needs to hand out good grades to under performing students to appease parents. As a result the material in schools gets easier and easier, and students stop learning what they need to learn because certain students hold entire classes back.
Then there's the issue of more behavior problems in schools today. Parenting has deteriorated so much that the majority of classes often deal with little more than keeping problem students in check. When the teacher calls the parents they go into denial about their child being disobedient- refusing to address the problem.

